   "textLength": 1056,
   "text": "AI coding agents are only as good as what they know about your project. When you need general information or libraries, the pre-learned knowledge is often good enough. For specialized tasks, the agent is working with thin coverage at best and confidently wrong assumptions at worst. When coding, the result can look plausible, but parameter names can be wrong or even be borrowed from a different lib",
